        "content": "<p>HI All -- a lot has changed with AI and formalization since starting this thread a year ago!  Just sharing <a href=\"https://github.com/jonhanke/quadratic-forms-lean\">quadratic-forms-lean</a> (<a href=\"https://github.com/jonhanke/quadratic-forms-lean/releases/tag/v0.1.0\">v0.1.0</a>), an AI-authored Lean 4 library on quadratic forms over number fields. Its main results are:</p>\n<p>- Hasse–Minkowski over number fields (isotropy, representation, isometry)<br>\n  - Hilbert reciprocity over number fields, by a local proof (no class field theory)<br>\n  - Siegel's theorem and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau(\\mathrm{SO}(Q)) = 2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1132em;\">τ</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">SO</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">Q</span><span class=\"mclose\">))</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span> with the mass formula over totally real number fields</p>\n<p>Details are in the <a href=\"#narrow/channel/583339-AI-authored-projects/topic/Quadratic.20forms.20.26.20Siegel.27s.20theorem.20for.20totally.20real.20.23.20fields/with/633419267\">#AI authored projects</a> thread. Feedback, and suggestions on what to bring into Mathlib or Tau Ceti, are very welcome!</p>\n<p>Thanks!<br>\n  -Jon</p>",
